    ("SG", "Politics", MARCUS,
     "Singapore estates let residents vote on how to spend upgrade funds",
     "Households in four estates chose between shade, seating and play areas.",
     [
         "Residents in 4 Singapore housing estates have voted on how to spend S$2.4 million set aside for neighbourhood upgrades, in a pilot of what officials call participatory budgeting.",
         "About 11,000 households in Tampines, Bukit Batok, Toa Payoh and Sengkang were sent a short list of projects and asked to rank them online or on paper forms at community centres.",
         "## What people chose",
         "Covered walkways to bus stops came first in 3 of the 4 estates. Shaded seating for older residents and new fitness corners followed. A proposal for a larger dog run in Sengkang won narrowly after a lively campaign by pet owners.",
         "“For years we complained at meetings and nothing seemed to happen,” said a retiree in Toa Payoh who helped hand out paper forms. “This time we could see the list, the cost of each item, and the result.”",
         "## Turnout",
         "Turnout averaged 38%, which organisers said was higher than they expected for a first attempt. It was lowest among households with young children and highest among residents over 60.",
         "## Limits",
         "Residents could only choose from projects already judged feasible by town council engineers, and the budget was a small fraction of what Singapore spends on estate upgrades each year.",
         "Some residents said the choices felt narrow. Political scientists said the pilot was modest but significant in a system where most planning decisions are made centrally, and that the real test would be whether residents could propose their own projects in future rounds.",
         "Work on the winning projects will begin in January, and the scheme may expand to 10 more estates in 2027.",
     ]),
